  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ケチョウセンアサガオ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B1%E3%83%81%E3%83%A7%E3%82%A6%E3%82%BB%E3%83%B3%E3%82%A2%E3%82%B5%E3%82%AC%E3%82%AA",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107862367,
      "text": "ケチョウセンアサガオ は、ナス科の種である。英名では thorn-apple・ downy thorn-apple・ Indian-apple 等別名が多い。北アメリカ原産。\n学名はしばしば D. innoxia として引用される。その D. inoxia との命名は、イギリスの植物学者フィリップ・ミラーが最初に1768年に種を記載したとき、ラテン語の innoxia（無害の意味）をスペルミスしたことによる。\nかつて、Datura meteloides という名が用いられていたが、今はその名は放棄されている。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Datura innoxia」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Datura_innoxia",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1353546768,
      "text": "Datura innoxia, known as pricklyburr, recurved thorn-apple, downy thorn-apple, Indian-apple, lovache, moonflower, nacazcul, toloatzin, toloaxihuitl, tolguache or toloache, is a species of flowering plant in the family Solanaceae. It is more rarely called sacred datura, a common name which is applied more often to the closely related Datura wrightii. It is native to the Southwestern United States, Central and South America, and introduced in Africa, Asia, Australia and Europe. The scientific name is often cited as D. innoxia. When English botanist Philip Miller first described the species in 1768, he misspelled the Latin word innoxia (inoffensive) when naming it D. inoxia. The name Datura meteloides was for some time erroneously applied to some members of the species, but that name has now been abandoned."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "toxicity": {
      "ja": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ケチョウセンアサガオ」の節「毒性」",
        "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B1%E3%83%81%E3%83%A7%E3%82%A6%E3%82%BB%E3%83%B3%E3%82%A2%E3%82%B5%E3%82%AC%E3%82%AA#%E6%AF%92%E6%80%A7",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 107862367,
        "heading": "毒性",
        "text": "全体が有毒であり、摂取すると死に至ることがある。\n国や地域によっては、購入や売却、または育成することが禁止されている。",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Datura innoxia」の節「Toxicity」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Datura_innoxia#Toxicity",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1353546768,
        "heading": "Toxicity",
        "text": "All parts of Datura plants are toxic, containing dangerous levels of tropane alkaloids (hyoscyamine, hyoscine) and may be fatal if ingested by humans and other animals, including livestock and pets. The main observed effects of ingestion are enlarged pupils, dry mouth, trouble breathing, blurred vision, hallucinations, panic, death. In some places, it is prohibited to buy, sell or cultivate Datura plants.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
